  "notes": "This feature is a behavior change (migration) to an existing API, so the inventory is the migration itself plus the three read surfaces whose values it changes: the deviceMemory property (one mixin, exposed on Navigator and WorkerNavigator — documented as one item on one child route), the Sec-CH-Device-Memory client hint, and its deprecated Device-Memory alias (documented as a section of the Sec-CH child route since it is the same value under a legacy name). The bucket values trace to the M147 branch implementation (kMinMemory/kMaxMemory) and to BCD's own Chrome-147 notes on all four keys; the intent thread was read in full and the rollout history (Android 1GB restored 2026-01-27; disabled after the x.com incident 2026-02-13; re-enabled for 147 on 2026-02-23) is documented under #migration-lifecycle. github.com URLs (w3c/device-memory PR#53, issues #50/#24) are cited from the chromestatus record and intent thread verbatim; this sandbox's proxy blocks github.com HTML (403 for every repo), so they were verified via provenance and the repo's raw.githubusercontent mirror rather than a direct 200 check."
